<Page title="Beyond Tech" description="When I'm not building cloud platforms, I perform comedy magic.">

  <div class="section-header">
    <span class="section-header__eyebrow">Personal</span>
    <h1>Beyond Tech</h1>
  </div>

  <hr class="divider" />

  <section class="beyond">
    <p class="beyond__text">
      When I step away from cloud architecture and open-source code, I step onto the stage as a comedy magician. What began as a quiet personal curiosity slowly transformed into something far more meaningful—a creative outlet that lets me share genuine warmth, laughter, and wonder with people across all walks of life. From performing for diplomats at the embassies of Denmark, Germany, and Yemen, to touring with K(night) of Awkwardness (a traveling theater show honoring our shared human quirks), to performing live on News18 India, magic has taught me how deeply we all long to connect and be surprised.
    <p class="beyond__text">
      At first glance, standardizing Kubernetes clusters or automating GitOps pipelines feels worlds apart from misdirection and comedic timing. But underneath, both are powered by the exact same human element. Whether you are building resilient tech systems or crafting a stage routine, the heart of the craft is empathy. It is about reading the subtle shifts in the room, understanding the hidden mechanics beneath what people see, and turning moments of tension or uncertainty into lighthearted, unexpected joy. Tech builds the infrastructure that keeps our world running, but magic reminds us why those human connections matter in the first place.
    <p class="beyond__text">
      To learn more about my magic, comedy, explore upcoming show details visit:
    </p>
    <a href="https://whitecrowmagic.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="beyond__link">
      whitecrowmagic.com &rarr;
    </a>
  </section>

</Page>

